  "caption": "Quinn's futsal comeback came with groin pain that flared with sprinting, kicking and even sneezing. Dr Google said \"sports hernia\".\n\nDespite the name, it usually isn't a true hernia. The belly and inner-thigh muscles both pull near the pubic bone, and repeated sprinting, cutting and kicking can overload those tissues.\n\nWhat often helps: rest alone usually isn't enough, so build inner-thigh, core and hip strength step by step, then rebuild sprinting, cutting and kicking in that order. Steady rehab often takes a couple of months or more.\n\nA groin lump, fever, testicle pain or swelling, night pain, or pain after one big injury should be checked promptly.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
